# 15. ENCOUNTERS

Every actual facility visit shall be represented by an Encounter.

An encounter may be:

* Scheduled
* Unscheduled
* Emergency
* Follow-up
* Clinical review
* NCD screening
* Diagnostic visit
* Medication review

## 15.1 Important Rule

An appointment is not an encounter.

```text
Appointment
     │
     └── may result in
             │
          Encounter
```

An unscheduled patient may directly create an encounter.

---

# 16. UNSCHEDULED ENCOUNTERS

The system shall support unscheduled visits.

Examples:

* New symptoms
* Complications
* Abnormal laboratory result
* Medication problem
* Adverse reaction
* Emergency
* Walk-in
* Clinical deterioration
* Referral
* Patient-requested review

An unscheduled encounter shall not automatically replace an existing scheduled follow-up visit.

Example:

```text
Scheduled Month 3 Visit
        │
        ├── remains scheduled
        │
        └── Patient develops symptoms
                 │
                 └── Unscheduled Encounter
```

