Visit 2        Day 14
Visit 3        Day 30
Visit 4        Day 60
Visit 5        Day 90
Visit 6        Day 180
Visit 7        Day 365
```

---

# 28. FOLLOW-UP SCHEDULING MODES

## Automatic

The system generates visits automatically.

## Manual

Staff create and schedule visits manually.

## Hybrid

The system automatically generates visits while authorized staff can:

* Reschedule
* Add visits
* Cancel visits
* Skip visits
* Change future frequency
* Create unscheduled visits

Hybrid should be the preferred general mode.

---

# 29. ROLLING AUTOMATIC SCHEDULING

The system shall support generation of future visits without generating an unlimited schedule.

Example:

```text
Frequency: Every 1 Month
Generate Ahead: 3 Months
Maximum Future Visits: 3
```

System generates:

```text
October
November
December
```

January is not initially generated.

After October is completed:

```text
November
December
January
```

The system generates January automatically.

This maintains a rolling future schedule.

---

# 30. FOLLOW-UP REFERENCE DATE

The scheduling engine shall support:

* Baseline
* Last completed visit
* Custom date
* Custom month

Example:

```text
Baseline = 10 January
Frequency = Every 3 Months

10 April
10 July
10 October
```

Another patient may use:

```text
Last completed = 18 April
Frequency = Every 3 Months

18 July
18 October
```

---

# 31. FREQUENCY CHANGES

The system shall allow frequency changes over time.

Example:

```text
Every 3 Months
       ↓
Every 1 Month
       ↓
Every 3 Months
```

Changing the frequency shall affect future planned visits.

It shall not rewrite historical completed visits.

