# 39. ORGANIZATIONAL ACCESS LEVELS

## Facility Level

Users can access authorized data within assigned facilities.

## District Level

Users can access authorized data from facilities within their assigned district.

## Regional Level

Users can access authorized data across districts/facilities within their assigned region.

## Zonal Level

Users can access authorized data across regions within their assigned zone.

## Country Level

Authorized users can access data across the country.

---

# 40. DISEASE-BASED ACCESS

Users may have access to one or more diseases.

Example:

```text
User A
Role: Regional Diabetes Coordinator
Region: Region A
Disease: Diabetes
```

The user can access authorized Diabetes information in Region A but does not automatically gain access to:

* Cardiac data
* Sickle Cell data
* Other regions

Another user may have:

```text
Disease Scope:
All NCDs
```

---

# 41. MODULE-BASED ACCESS

Users shall only access modules required for their responsibilities.

Example:

```text
Laboratory Staff
    │
    └── Laboratory
```

They should not automatically receive access to:

* Pharmacy administration
* Inventory administration
* User administration
* NCD configuration

unless explicitly authorized.

