# 67. IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULES

### Rule 1

A patient may have multiple NCD conditions.

### Rule 2

A patient does not have to be enrolled in every NCD program.

### Rule 3

Clinical services are shared across diseases.

### Rule 4

An appointment is not an encounter.

### Rule 5

An unscheduled encounter does not automatically replace a scheduled follow-up visit.

### Rule 6

Completed clinical records should not normally be deleted.

### Rule 7

Future visits without clinical data may be modified according to authorization.

### Rule 8

Changing future frequency must not rewrite historical visits.

### Rule 9

Access must be enforced at the data level, not only in the UI.

### Rule 10

Disease access does not automatically grant access to other diseases.

### Rule 11

Module access does not automatically grant access to other modules.

### Rule 12

A lower-level user cannot access records outside their organizational scope.

### Rule 13

Higher-level access must still respect disease and module permissions.

### Rule 14

All sensitive access changes and exports must be audited.

### Rule 15

New NCD diseases should be addable without redesigning the entire platform.

